      "prompt": "Edit target image1 six-frame sprite sheet. Change ONLY TWO cells: TOP RIGHT cell3 and BOTTOM LEFT cell4. Keep other fourcells/heads/torso/armor/colors/scale/transparentbackground exactly unchanged. This is a walk cycle with wrongly repeated sameleg. In TOP RIGHT cell3, SWAP both leg and arm poses: visible LIGHT NEAR leg (with moss on its kneeplate) must extend BACKWARD to LEFT of hips with heel raised; DARK FAR leg must extend FORWARD to RIGHT of hips and plant foot. The near LIGHT arm must swing FORWARD to RIGHT, and far DARK arm BACKWARD to LEFT. In BOTTOM LEFT cell4, visible LIGHT NEAR leg bends behind hips toward LEFT, lifted off ground; DARK FAR leg vertical planted supporting underhip. Near LIGHT arm swings forwardRIGHT. CRITICAL: do not keep mossy near knee/foot forward in cell3; mossy near knee must be BEHIND hips at LEFT while dark far knee is in FRONT atRIGHT. Both leg silhouettes visible and anatomically connected through root hips. Preserve allothercells. No new background, labels or additional characters. Genuine alpha. Two legs only, no extra arms.",
